    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0078" n="41" xml:id="pg41"/>

                <head>20. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Brzezinski) to President Carter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d20-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-02-21">February 21, 1978</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to your enclosed note regarding help and/or communication with
                        Savimbi,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d20-f2"/> I have asked the CIA to respond to a
                    number of specific questions. Their response is herewith attached.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d20-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have marked on pages 2–4 certain limited actions we could undertake to enhance
                    our communications with Savimbi and to provide him some limited indirect help.
                    None of them would involve major engagement of U.S. resources or prestige, yet
                    cumulatively they could upgrade his capabilities.</p>
                <p>We will be considering this matter in the SCC,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d20-f4"/> but
                    given your personal initiative, I thought I would respond immediately.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d20-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d20-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material,
                    Brzezinski Office File, Country Chron File, Box 2, Angola: 1977–1978. Secret;
                    Sensitive. Carter wrote at the top of the memorandum: “What help is other
                    nations <hi rendition="#italic">giving</hi>? C.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d20-f2" n="2" xml:id="d20-f2-content">
                <p>Not found attached.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d20-f3" n="3" xml:id="d20-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d19">Document 19</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d20-f4" n="4" xml:id="d20-f4-content">
                <p> Carter underlined “considering this matter in the SCC,” and wrote “good” in the
                    right-hand margin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
